       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **The order as written:** metformin 4,250 mg three times daily comes to **12,750 mg/day**.\n- **The usual maximum:** the FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day. The order is about 5 times the labeled maximum.\n- **The risk:** a dose this high carries a serious risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- **425 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals (a possible typo, or a lower starting dose)\n- **1,000 mg** by mouth twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n\nIf you really do want 4,250 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it was intentional. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
